--- Comment #4 from Stuart Bennett <sb476-KWPb1pKIrIJaa/9Udqfwiw@public.gmane.org>  2009-01-13 14:54:01 PST ---
This is almost certainly not a nouveau bug (since it works with the xrandr
tool).  I suggest you look at http://wiki.debian.org/XStrikeForce/HowToRandR12
to fix your configuration; for instance you need to use `Identifier
"Monitor-VGA-0"' instead of `Identifier "VGA-0"' etc.  Also note that DVI-D-0
is probably DVI-I-0 these days.


